-- title:
--   Drinfeld chart at a supersingular point with equivariant linear parts
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $q\ell$, with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, $\xi \in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity and $\zeta = \xi^{\ell}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$, and let $K \subseteq L((t))$ be the subfield generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly with the tower $A \to L \to K$, let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $z$ be a point of the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak{X} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout of the two maps out of `XMid`, built from the subalgebras of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, respectively over $A[j^{-1}]$) at which the germ of $\varpi$, pulled back along the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk; let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the finite chart algebra with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y) = z$, and assume that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$ one has $\varphi(j) \in$ [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point. Then there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$ (a domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal), a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with maximal ideal of $W$ generated by $\sigma\varpi$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $$e : \widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{\mathfrak{X},z} \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\,C(\sigma\varpi)\,v - f\,u\,),$$ where the completion is the adic completion of the stalk at its maximal ideal, such that: (i) for every $a \in A$, $e$ sends the image in the completion of the germ of $a$ to the class of the constant $C(\sigma a)$; and (ii) for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \subseteq SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) (for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f_0, g_0$ of weight $k$ and level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions and $g_0 \neq 0$, all $x \in K$ whose expansion is the image of the quotient of those $q$-expansions, and all embeddings $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta = e^{2\pi i/q}$, one has $\iota(\tau x) \cdot q\text{-exp}(g_0 \mid_k c_q(\gamma^{-1})) = q\text{-exp}(f_0 \mid_k c_q(\gamma^{-1}))$, with $c_q$ as in `conjElemN`), if $\tau$ preserves the finite chart algebra and its restriction there fixes $y$ modulo $y$ (that is, $\tau a - a \in y$ for all $a$), then there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in \mathrm{M}_2(W)$ such that $\theta$ intertwines $e$ and the action of $\tau$ on germs from the finite chart, $\theta$ fixes all constants $C(w)$, $\theta(X_{j}) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij} X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0, X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W$, $c \equiv 1$ modulo that ideal whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity.
--
--   This gives the Drinfeld-type local equation $\varpi v = f u$ with $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ for the completed local ring of the integral model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ at a supersingular point in characteristic $q$, together with the normalisation of the constants from $A$ and the description of the linear part of a level automorphism as $c\gamma$ with $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$. The present form is the corresponding chart statement without the branch-anchor clause, valid for all $q$ (in particular for $q \in \{2,3\}$); it is cited in the construction of the level-automorphism riders at such a point and in the identification of the relevant stalk quotient as a discrete valuation ring.
